WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.912 --> 00:00:17.856
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:19.820
Hi, Stillwater.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.260
Whatcha doing?

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:22.520
Hello, Karl.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.530
I'm just about to have my lunch.

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:26.325
Would you like to join me?

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:26.825
OK.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.240
What are you having?

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.545
All of my favorite things.

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:40.450
This is called a bento.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:42.570
What's that?

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.220
It's called persimmon.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.930
Have you ever tried them?

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:46.560
No.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.340
Are they good?

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:50.430
Oh, I like them very much.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:53.760
But everyone likes
things differently.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.400
What happens if I
don't like them?

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.000
It can be fun to try new
things, even if in the end

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.700
we don't enjoy them.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:05.870
If you don't like
them, then you'll know.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:06.380
OK.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.660
I'll try some persimmon.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.400
Would you like chopsticks?

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:10.900
Sure.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.320
How do they work?

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.180
Here, I know a trick.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.620
They're like little
pinchy fingers.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.860
It's a little bit crunchy
like an apple and sweet.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.150
I like it.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.610
Would you like to
try something else?

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:46.190
I'd like to try everything.

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:49.040
Wonderful.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.080
This is seaweed.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.740
You mean from the ocean?

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.410
Yes, from the ocean.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:01.040
It's slippery and
crunchy at the same time.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:02.690
That is lotus root.

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:09.860
It doesn't taste like anything.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.270
Is this a carrot?

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:13.970
It's called gobo,
or burdock root.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:20.000
Well, it doesn't
taste like a carrot.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.800
It's salty.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:24.155
That ube, purple sweet potato.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:30.580
It tastes like a
potato, but sweet.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.630
Gomai, spinach with sesame.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.895
This tastes way better
than regular spinach.

00:02:37.895 --> 00:02:38.395
Tofu.

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:42.850
I've heard of tofu.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:43.840
It's squishy.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.820
I like it.

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:48.690
Is that spaghetti?

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:52.200
Those are soba noodles
made from buckwheat.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.805
You dip and slurp.

00:02:57.287 --> 00:02:59.130
It's cold and chewy.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:08.885
Ah, you saved umaboshi
for last, salted plums.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.360
They're an acquired taste.

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:19.100
But I'm proud of you for trying.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.540
I'm proud of me too.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:23.810
I'm going to try new
things all the time now.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:27.440
I might find a new favorite
food like persimmons.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.810
Do you have any more?

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:30.800
I do indeed.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:41.050
[MUSIC PLAYING]

